# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# revault — client-only Next.js site. The backend (intake form, page-view
# analytics + their admin API) lives in the shared platform server
# (../ruudjuffermans-server → api.ruudjuffermans.nl) as the "revault" module;
# INTAKE_EMAIL, SMTP_* and ADMIN_SERVICE_TOKEN live in that project's env.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# --- Client (Next.js; NEXT_PUBLIC_* is baked in at build time) ---
# Platform API origin. Leave EMPTY in dev: the browser then calls same-origin
# /api/* and next.config.ts rewrites it to the local platform server on :4000.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=
# Canonical site URL (metadata + www→apex redirect).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3001
